<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upolu</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Upolu is the second-largest and most populous island of Samoa, home to the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apia">Apia</a>. Its high chiefly titles were central to Samoan politics, and in the 19th century Apia became the base of rival German, British and American interests. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripartite-convention-1899">Tripartite Convention of 1899</a> it became part of German Samoa, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a> occupied it in 1914, before Samoa's independence in 1962.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/upolu.jpg" alt="Upolu" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CloudSurfer at English Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Samoa_Country_map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
